WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:05.560
Sprinkle salt on cucumber slices.

2
00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:09.580
In about fifteen minutes, drops of water bead up on top.

3
00:00:10.420 --> 00:00:12.400
Put limp lettuce in plain cold water.

4
00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:15.760
In about fifteen minutes, it can turn crisp again.

5
00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:19.640
Nobody pushes the water, and the cells do not pump it.

6
00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:21.940
So how does it move, and which way?

7
00:00:22.933 --> 00:00:25.073
Drop food colouring into still water.

8
00:00:25.953 --> 00:00:27.593
At first, it sits in one spot.

9
00:00:28.733 --> 00:00:31.933
Concentration is how much of a substance is in a given space.

10
00:00:32.653 --> 00:00:35.473
Where the drop landed, the dye is highly concentrated.

11
00:00:36.453 --> 00:00:37.533
Far away, it is low.

12
00:00:38.373 --> 00:00:40.393
The particles are always moving at random.

13
00:00:41.293 --> 00:00:43.333
More leave the crowded spot than enter it.

14
00:00:43.973 --> 00:00:44.973
So the dye spreads.

15
00:00:45.967 --> 00:00:51.207
Diffusion is the movement of a substance from where it is more concentrated to where

16
00:00:51.207 --> 00:00:52.387
it is less concentrated.

17
00:00:53.527 --> 00:00:54.527
Now the dye is even.

18
00:00:55.207 --> 00:00:56.467
The particles do not stop.

19
00:00:57.307 --> 00:00:59.347
Just as many move one way as the other.

20
00:01:00.167 --> 00:01:01.447
So the colour stops changing.

21
00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:05.760
The cell membrane is the thin layer around every cell.

22
00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:08.040
It is selectively permeable.

23
00:01:08.760 --> 00:01:11.020
It lets some things through and holds back others.

24
00:01:11.980 --> 00:01:15.940
In most cells, water, oxygen and carbon dioxide cross easily.

25
00:01:16.860 --> 00:01:20.900
Many dissolved particles, such as salt and sugar, cross much less easily.

26
00:01:21.860 --> 00:01:26.280
Oxygen is more concentrated in the blood than inside a cell, so it diffuses in.

27
00:01:27.250 --> 00:01:32.230
Osmosis is the diffusion of water across a selectively permeable membrane.

28
00:01:33.230 --> 00:01:36.570
Dissolve salt in water, and the water there is less concentrated.

29
00:01:37.630 --> 00:01:40.110
Water moves toward the side with more dissolved salt.

30
00:01:41.030 --> 00:01:45.650
Many dissolved particles cannot follow, so the difference stays and the water keeps

31
00:01:45.650 --> 00:01:49.550
moving that way. Our model membrane holds back all the salt.

32
00:01:50.450 --> 00:01:52.810
Most real ones let some through, much more slowly.

33
00:01:53.833 --> 00:01:55.393
Now the cucumber makes sense.

34
00:01:56.513 --> 00:02:00.953
Salt outside means the water outside is less concentrated, so water leaves the

35
00:02:00.953 --> 00:02:06.213
cells. In lettuce, each cell holds more dissolved particles than plain water, so

36
00:02:06.213 --> 00:02:09.973
water moves in. Neither time do the cells spend energy.

37
00:02:10.813 --> 00:02:12.073
That is passive transport.

38
00:02:13.033 --> 00:02:17.013
Water moves toward more dissolved particles, and the cell spends no energy.
